{
  "dom_id": "step-q5984",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The length of the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ on $[2,4]$ is given by",
  "worked_solution": "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{\u2032}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=2{x}^{2},$ $a=2,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=4x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{\u2032}(x)=4x$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{\u2032}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+(4x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
